course: dictionary
lesson: 10712
title: Untrue and how it works
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Untrue means not true. It is the opposite of true, so an untrue statement does not match the facts. «A rumour can be untrue, and even a true one can hurt.» A rumour is a story passed around from person to person, and it may be false.
explain: You can often make an opposite by adding un- to the front of a word: true becomes untrue, kind becomes unkind. The small part added to the start of a word is called a prefix, so un- is a prefix that means not.
explain: Watch out for two nots. «It's not untrue» means «it's true», because the two nots cancel each other out. When a sentence has two negatives, read it slowly and check which way it points.
fact: Untrue is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «untrue rumours».
fact: «Untrue» means not true; false or wrong.
fact: In old or poetic use, «untrue» means not loyal or faithful to someone.
fact: An untrue statement does not match the facts; in science and maths it can be checked and found untrue.
fact: «Many untrue stories are not lies», because memory fills its gaps by guessing, so two honest people can remember the same thing differently.
exercise: «A rumour can be untrue, and even a true one can hurt.» What does untrue mean here? | Loyal and faithful to a friend | Very true and correct | Loud and clear | *Not true; false or wrong
exercise: Which word means the same as untrue? | heavy | kind | brave | *false
exercise: «Many untrue stories are not lies: memory fills its gaps by guessing.» Why can a story be untrue without anyone lying? | Because the teller wanted to hurt someone | Because it is always written in a book | Because it is a poem | *Because memory guesses to fill gaps, so honest people can get facts wrong
test: «It's not untrue» means what? | It is a rumour | *It is true | It is a poem | It is false
test: In old or poetic use, what does untrue mean? | Quite cold | Very loud | *Not loyal or faithful to someone | Very old
exam: «If you passed on something untrue, what should you do?» | Laugh and tell another rumour | Tell it to more people to be sure | *Go back to the people you told, say it was not true, and say sorry | Ignore it and hope nobody noticed
